WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.296 --> 00:00:16.179
was taken to the home of the boy, Dag.

2
00:00:17.239 --> 00:00:20.562
His house had stone walls and a roof made of straw.

3
00:00:21.763 --> 00:00:25.046
His mother and sister, Birgitta, were inside.

4
00:00:26.106 --> 00:00:27.868
Dag explained what happened.

5
00:00:32.088 --> 00:00:35.150
Dag and Gunnar laid Vinnie down on a bench.

6
00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:38.192
It was covered with bear skins.

7
00:00:39.213 --> 00:00:41.395
Dag's mother hurried over to Vinnie.

8
00:00:41.415 --> 00:00:46.418
"Birgitta, bring me the whale bone," she said.

9
00:00:46.438 --> 00:00:50.021
"Whale bone?"

10
00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:51.302
asked Mandy.

11
00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:53.403
"What is that for?

12
00:00:53.423 --> 00:00:56.245
Is Vinnie going to be okay?"

13
00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:59.948
"Don't worry," said Dag's mother.

14
00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:04.650
"There are magic symbols carved into the whale bone.

15
00:01:05.851 --> 00:01:08.333
It will help your brother heal quickly."

16
00:01:09.374 --> 00:01:12.015
Birgitta gave the whale bone to her mother.

17
00:01:13.236 --> 00:01:16.719
Her mother placed it under the bear skins beneath Vinnie.

18
00:01:17.879 --> 00:01:20.961
Vikings believed that symbols had magical power.

19
00:01:23.243 --> 00:01:25.785
Soon after, Vinnie opened his eyes.

20
00:01:25.805 --> 00:01:30.268
"Oh, my head," he groaned.

21
00:01:31.208 --> 00:01:33.329
There was a big bump on his forehead.

22
00:01:34.209 --> 00:01:35.390
He tried to sit up.

23
00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.431
"Where am I?

24
00:01:37.951 --> 00:01:39.212
Where's my sister?"

25
00:01:40.592 --> 00:01:42.653
Mandy knelt down beside Vinnie.

26
00:01:42.673 --> 00:01:44.894
"Are you okay?"

27
00:01:45.374 --> 00:01:45.935
she asked.

28
00:01:45.955 --> 00:01:50.297
"Except for a headache, yes," he replied.

29
00:01:51.117 --> 00:01:53.518
Mandy turned to Birgitta and Dag's mother.

30
00:01:53.538 --> 00:01:57.500
"Thank you so much," she said.

31
00:02:00.272 --> 00:02:05.735
Now that Vinnie seemed better, Mandy looked at the inside of the house more closely.

32
00:02:06.756 --> 00:02:09.997
It was just one long room with no windows.

33
00:02:10.978 --> 00:02:13.639
In the middle of the room was a fireplace.

34
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:22.844
She was surprised to see animals—a cow, two sheep, and four pigs—in a pen at the far end

35
00:02:22.924 --> 00:02:23.525
of the house.

36
00:02:23.545 --> 00:02:27.887
"Why do the animals live in your house?"

37
00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:29.808
she asked Birgitta.

38
00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.224
"It's too cold to keep them outdoors," she explained.

39
00:02:34.244 --> 00:02:37.968
"And having them inside keeps us warm too."

40
00:02:37.988 --> 00:02:45.295
"Birgitta," called her mother, "take this soup to our old neighbor Hilda.

41
00:02:45.896 --> 00:02:47.938
She's been sick for three days."

42
00:02:48.818 --> 00:02:50.680
Birgitta took the pot of soup.

43
00:02:51.541 --> 00:02:54.044
"Come with me," she said to Mandy.

44
00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:00.662
While the girls were gone, Vinnie watched Gunnar practice sword fighting with Dag.

45
00:03:01.843 --> 00:03:03.363
They used wooden swords.

46
00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:07.465
"Gunnar, do you really want to be a warrior?"

47
00:03:08.425 --> 00:03:09.086
asked Vinnie.

48
00:03:09.106 --> 00:03:12.467
"Yes, I do," Gunnar said.

49
00:03:12.487 --> 00:03:15.968
"I practice my fighting skills whenever I can.

50
00:03:17.069 --> 00:03:19.970
There is nothing better than being a Viking warrior.

51
00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.911
I want to be the next Leif Erikson!"

52
00:03:22.931 --> 00:03:24.252
"Who's that?"

53
00:03:24.856 --> 00:03:25.536
asked Vinnie.

54
00:03:25.556 --> 00:03:27.897
"You don't know about him?"

55
00:03:28.578 --> 00:03:30.058
said Gunnar, surprised.

56
00:03:30.979 --> 00:03:33.460
"He's one of our most famous explorers.

57
00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:38.022
Leif Erikson discovered a new land far across the sea.

58
00:03:38.942 --> 00:03:40.923
He and his men saw many forests.

59
00:03:41.763 --> 00:03:44.324
The wood was perfect for building longships.

60
00:03:45.185 --> 00:03:47.226
They said the fish were bigger than me!"

61
00:03:51.047 --> 00:03:52.468
Vinnie and Gunnar laughed.

62
00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.922
Then they heard a loud noise at the door.

63
00:03:55.942 --> 00:04:00.164
"I finally found you little ship rats!"

64
00:04:00.905 --> 00:04:02.126
yelled Skull-Crusher.

65
00:04:02.146 --> 00:04:03.547
"My Captain!"

66
00:04:04.347 --> 00:04:05.748
Gunnar bowed his head.

67
00:04:07.629 --> 00:04:10.231
The red-faced captain stood in the doorway.

68
00:04:11.171 --> 00:04:12.632
He was very angry.

69
00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:15.734
"Where is my good-luck charm?"

70
00:04:16.415 --> 00:04:17.836
Skull-Crusher demanded.
